WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.438 --> 00:00:18.482
Without warning, the children landed at the bottom of a tunnel with a loud thud.

2
00:00:18.502 --> 00:00:21.865
“Ouch!” shouted Vinnie.

3
00:00:21.885 --> 00:00:24.508
“Oomph!” cried Mandy.

4
00:00:25.549 --> 00:00:26.670
They opened their eyes.

5
00:00:27.891 --> 00:00:29.192
The bright light was gone.

6
00:00:30.248 --> 00:00:32.309
The darkness of the tunnel was gone, too.

7
00:00:33.269 --> 00:00:36.370
They both lay on the ground, not far from each other.

8
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.010
“Are you okay?”

9
00:00:39.571 --> 00:00:40.851
Vinnie called to his sister.

10
00:00:41.651 --> 00:00:44.032
They had landed on the bank of a long river.

11
00:00:44.972 --> 00:00:47.173
They could see ducks and geese flying by.

12
00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:51.954
Men with nets and spears were fishing from boats and from land.

13
00:00:51.974 --> 00:00:55.875
“Mandy?” Vinnie called to her again.

14
00:00:56.835 --> 00:01:02.302
As he got up and moved closer to Mandy, Vinnie could see why she didn’t answer.

15
00:01:03.283 --> 00:01:06.225
Standing in front of her was a boy about Vinnie’s age.

16
00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:08.607
He was dark and slender.

17
00:01:08.627 --> 00:01:12.510
“Are you the gods of the Nile?”

18
00:01:13.331 --> 00:01:15.152
the boy asked, falling to his knees.

19
00:01:15.172 --> 00:01:17.174
“The Nile?”

20
00:01:17.614 --> 00:01:18.535
Vinnie questioned.

21
00:01:19.356 --> 00:01:21.057
Then he realized where they were.

22
00:01:21.077 --> 00:01:23.319
“We’re in Egypt!”

23
00:01:23.359 --> 00:01:24.600
he shouted at Mandy.

24
00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.389
“Please don’t hurt me,” the strange boy cried, his voice shaking.

25
00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:34.573
“No, we are not gods,” Vinnie said to the boy.

26
00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:38.336
“I’m Vinnie and this is my sister, Mandy.”

27
00:01:39.657 --> 00:01:44.961
The stranger wore only a short white skirt, tied with a sash around his waist.

28
00:01:46.102 --> 00:01:48.484
Suddenly Vinnie looked down at himself.

29
00:01:49.685 --> 00:01:51.327
That’s all he was wearing, too!

30
00:01:52.428 --> 00:01:53.949
Vinnie’s face turned red.

31
00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.052
Mandy was also dressed differently.

32
00:01:58.208 --> 00:02:00.869
Her body was covered by a straight white dress.

33
00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.330
Her feet were in sandals.

34
00:02:04.111 --> 00:02:05.891
Her hair was in a long braid.

35
00:02:05.911 --> 00:02:12.174
“But I saw you fall from the sky,” said the boy, getting back up on his feet.

36
00:02:12.194 --> 00:02:18.216
“We have special powers,” she paused and looked at Vinnie.

37
00:02:19.097 --> 00:02:22.938
He was still holding the photograph, which he stuck inside his sash.

38
00:02:23.999 --> 00:02:26.780
The stranger gasped and fell to his knees again.

39
00:02:27.864 --> 00:02:28.625
“Don’t worry.

40
00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:32.328
We’re not going to hurt you,” Mandy said kindly.

41
00:02:32.348 --> 00:02:34.329
“We need your help.”

42
00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:39.413
“I am Akhom,” the boy said, “and I promise to help you.”

43
00:02:39.433 --> 00:02:42.836
“Thank you, Akhom,” said Mandy.

44
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.899
They heard voices coming toward them from the distance.

45
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.401
Vinnie and Mandy froze.

46
00:02:49.421 --> 00:02:53.845
“Oh, those are my friends,” Akhom explained.

47
00:02:54.846 --> 00:02:57.368
He held up an odd shaped ball in his hand.

48
00:02:58.432 --> 00:03:00.013
“I left them to look for my ball.

49
00:03:00.373 --> 00:03:01.394
Then I saw you.”

50
00:03:03.175 --> 00:03:05.096
Vinnie and Mandy looked at each other.

51
00:03:05.116 --> 00:03:10.038
“Please don’t tell them about us, Akhom,” they both said.

52
00:03:10.579 --> 00:03:11.299
Akhom nodded.

53
00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:13.801
“Yes, it would be best for you to hide.

54
00:03:14.741 --> 00:03:16.862
My friends are not accustomed to strangers.”

55
00:03:18.143 --> 00:03:19.764
The loud shouts came nearer.

56
00:03:19.784 --> 00:03:23.686
“Akhom! Are you looking for cobras again?”

57
00:03:24.326 --> 00:03:25.287
shouted one boy.

58
00:03:25.307 --> 00:03:28.581
“Cobras?” whispered Vinnie.

59
00:03:29.602 --> 00:03:32.444
Vinnie hated snakes even more than spiders.

60
00:03:32.464 --> 00:03:36.047
“Cobras, hippos, crocodiles.

61
00:03:36.488 --> 00:03:40.051
They’re all over the Nile,” Akhom whispered back.

62
00:03:40.071 --> 00:03:45.735
“Crocodiles!” Vinnie mouthed, his eyes getting very big.

63
00:03:45.755 --> 00:03:49.839
“Akhom! Where are you?”

64
00:03:50.479 --> 00:03:55.784
the voices shouted again Akhom threw the ball back to his friends.

65
00:03:57.308 --> 00:03:59.290
Then he signaled to Vinnie and Mandy.

66
00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.592
“Quickly follow me!”

67
00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:06.217
Vinnie and Mandy ran after him.

68
00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:13.824
Out of breath, they arrived at a small house with windows high up on the walls.

69
00:04:14.585 --> 00:04:17.608
Its white surface had many cracks from the hot sun.

70
00:04:17.628 --> 00:04:21.812
“Welcome to my home,” Akhom said warmly.
